{"id": "mm6421a4", "status": "ok", "message_id": "msg_011CggGVWfUbuRK64Hqo69Sx", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "errors": [], "usage": {"input": 14563, "output": 4522}, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "```json\n{\"id\": \"mm6421a4\",\n \"data_focus\": {\"v\": \"yes\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"CDC analyzed data from the 2013 National Health Interview Survey (NHIS)\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Among adults with multiple chronic conditions, those with arthritis had significantly higher prevalences of all the selected life domain outcomes than those without arthritis\"}]},\n \"outcome_types\": [{\"v\": \"binary/categorical\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Model-adjusted prevalences of all three life domain outcomes increased stepwise among adults with no chronic conditions\"}]}],\n \"analytic_depth\": [\n   {\"v\": \"summary\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The overall unadjusted prevalences of social participation restriction, serious psychological distress, and work disability in the U.S. adult population were 4.2%, 3.8%, and 12.8%\"}]},\n   {\"v\": \"comparison\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Among adults with multiple chronic conditions, those with arthritis had significantly higher prevalences of all the selected life domain outcomes than those without arthritis\"}]},\n   {\"v\": \"stratified/adjusted\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Adjusted for age group, sex, race/ethnicity, education attainment level, body mass index category, and smoking status.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Multivariate binary and multinomial logistic regressions were performed\"}]}\n ],\n \"study_design\": [{\"v\": \"cross-sectional\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"because of the cross-sectional nature of NHIS, temporal relationships cannot be established\"}]}],\n \"methods_quotes\": [\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Prevalence estimates (percentage with 95% confidence intervals [CIs]) were age-standardized using the year 2000 projected U.S. population\"},\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Multivariate binary and multinomial logistic regressions were performed\"},\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"were used to estimate prevalences of outcomes adjusting for the six covariates\"},\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"pairwise comparisons of model-adjusted proportions between adults with and without arthritis among those with one or more chronic conditions were performed\"},\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"two-sided alpha-level adjusting for multiple comparisons (Bonferroni correction p<0.001)\"},\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Taylor series linearization method was used to estimate standard errors and account for intracluster correlation because of the complex sampling design.\"}\n ],\n \"confidence\": \"high\",\n \"uncertain_fields\": []}\n```", "type": "text"}]}